    {
     "id": "deponentVerbs",
     "title": "Deponent Verbs",
     "titleLink": "deponent",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "para",
       "text": "Deponent verbs are verbs that are middle in form but translated as actives. They have no active form and are easy to tell in vocabulary lists because they have the middle ending -ομαι."
      },
      {
       "type": "para",
       "text": "Mounce notes that in the New Testament about 75% of the middle forms are deponent (p. 149).",
       "gapBefore": true
      },
      {
       "type": "para",
       "text": "Because of the deponent phenomena, middle forms may frequently be translated as actives (3 to 1). Many [[link:frequentVerbs]]frequent verbs[[/link]] are deponent.",
       "gapBefore": true
      },
      {
       "type": "para",
       "text": "When parsing a deponent verb, rather than listing the voice as active/middle/ passive, the verb is said to be deponent (e.g. present deponent indicative 1 sg).",
       "gapBefore": true
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "accompanyingCases",
     "title": "Accompanying Cases",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "para",
       "text": "Often with passives there is a need to express the agent, instrument, or means by which the subject is acted on."
      },
      {
       "type": "para",
       "text": "This is accomplished by:",
       "gapBefore": true
      },
      {
       "type": "numbered",
       "items": [
        "using ὑπό or διά with the genitive to expresses agency (e.g. Elliott was hit [[u]]by Zach.[[/u]]) or",
        "using the dative case to indicate means or instrument. The translation will use \"with\" or \"by\" (e.g. Elliott was hit [[u]]by the ball[[/u]].)."
       ],
       "gapBefore": true
      }
     ],
     "greekTaps": true
    },
    {
     "id": "compoundVerbs",
     "title": "Compound Verbs",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "para",
       "text": "As with other verbs, prepositions are often prefixed to deponent verbs to form a compound."
      },
      {
       "type": "greekRows",
       "layout": "compoundVerbs",
       "rows": [
        {
